 Clinical Informatics\, Dana-Farber Cancer Institute\n12:30 - 1:00  Student
  Research Topics: open discussion\n\nAbout the speaker: Manuel Fanarjian i
 s a palliative care physician and the Director of Clinical Informatics at 
 Dana-Farber Cancer Institute. Prior to a career in medicine\, he was a bio
 medical engineer\, and has industry experience in medical devices and digi
 tal health technologies. He is a graduate of Duke University and UNC Schoo
 l of Medicine and did his post-graduate training at the University of Penn
 sylvania (Internal Medicine) and Massachusetts General Hospital/Brigham & 
 Women's Hospital (Hospice and Palliative Medicine). He additionally comple
 ted a Biodesign fellowship at Harvard Medical School\, and he has a deep i
 nterest in adapting systems of care delivery in ways that improve the expe
 rience of patients and families\, as well as the clinicians and staff who 
 serve them.\n\nJoin on Microsoft Teams: https://teams.microsoft.com/l/meet
